 context of the problem, "valid approach" may mean a logically sound and correct path toward the solution.\n\nTherefore, i1 is the only one that follows a correct and plausible path.\n\nThe others either:\n- Use incorrect multipliers (e.g., 59*16)\n- Fail to build the required sub-expressions\n- Have no clear path\n\nThus, i1 is the only unique, valid approach.\n\nFinal selection: i1.\n</reasoning>\n<results>\ni1\n</results>']
