hrough near-multiples and failing to form a valid expression using all numbers — they represent the same incorrect approach. Neither is a valid solution, and both are redundant duplicates in terms of method and reasoning.\n\nTherefore, no valid or unique approach is present in the given partial solutions. All approaches are incomplete, lack a concrete expression, and fail to use the numbers to achieve the target.\n\nAs per the task, we are to identify the unique, valid approaches. Since no valid approach exists in the given set, and all partial solutions are incorrect and redundant, there are no valid ones to select.\n\nThus, no indices should be included in the output.\n</reasoning>\n<results>\n</results>']
