h are the same, we must pick one.\n\nThus, we select i0 as the representative, as it is the first occurrence of the method, and serves as the unique (though flawed) representation in the set.\n\nNote: The actual solution may not exist with the given constraints, but the task is to evaluate the partial solutions, not solve them. The evaluation shows both are identical in approach and invalid in outcome.\n\n</reasoning>\n<results>\ni0\n</results>']
